y object in message else loads the complete entity object","s":"Properties","u":"/Procify_Documentation/docs/Docs/API Document Link/Class EndPointBean","h":"#properties","p":5},{"i":14,"t":"addDependantEntities(entity): KloEntity[] Parameters​ Name Type Description entity KloEntity The KloEntity instance to add as a dependent entity Returns​ KloEntity[] - Array of all dependent entities including the newly added one Description​ Adds a dependent entity to be included in the data message sent to endpoints. Dependent entities are additional entities that should be sent along with the main entity object. This is useful when you need to send related data that may not be directly linked but is contextually important. Example​ let endpointBean = eventContext.addEndpoint(\"USER001\", EndpointType.USER, ChannelType.DEVICE, orderEntity); let customerEntity = await txn.loadEntityP(\"d_customer\", customerKey); endpointBean.addDependantEntities(customerEntity); // Customer info sent along with order See​ getDependantEntities to retrieve the list of dependent entities","s":"addDependantEntities","u":"/Procify_Documentation/docs/Docs/API Document Link/Class EndPointBean","h":"#adddependantentities","p":5},{"i":16,"t":"getDependantEntities(): KloEntity[] Returns​ KloEntity[] - Array of KloEntity instances that are configured as dependent entities Description​ Gets the list of dependent entities that have been added to this endpoint bean. Dependent entities are additional entities that will be included in the data message along with the primary entity object when the message is sent to endpoints. Example​ let endpointBean = eventContext.addEndpoint(\"USER001\", EndpointType.USER, ChannelType.DEVICE, orderEntity); endpointBean.addDependantEntities(customerEntity); endpointBean.addDependantEntities(productEntity); let dependents = endpointBean.getDependantEntities(); console.log(\"Number of dependent entities:\", dependents.length); See​ addDependantEntities to add dependent entitie